# Task 2 – ADR Reporting & Documentation

## Objective

To complete a structured Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR) reporting form based on the patient case identified in Task 1, following the principles of accurate, structured, and appropriate pharmacovigilance documentation.

---

## Case Summary

A 45-year-old female patient was prescribed amoxicillin, which was started 5 days prior to reporting. The patient subsequently developed rash, itching, nausea, and dizziness.

The patient was also taking paracetamol as needed.

Based on the temporal relationship between initiation of amoxicillin and the onset of the reported symptoms, amoxicillin was identified as the suspected medicine.

